# Knowledge Check {hideTitle}

## Knowledge Check

This module focuses on core safety decisions and response sequence.

::: group Checkpoint Group {mode=all showResultsSummary passingScore=80 pointsOverride=20 requireAll level=2}
::: choice What should happen first after a serious hazard is found? {points=2 required shuffle}
( ) Continue work and monitor
feedback: Monitoring matters, but immediate hazard control comes first.
(x) Stop work and secure the area
feedback: Correct. Immediate control reduces risk quickly.
( ) Wait until end-of-shift review
:::
::: choice Select all required pre-task checks {points=3 shuffle}
[x] PPE is inspected
feedback: Correct. Equipment inspection is required before every task.
[x] Exit routes are clear
feedback: Correct. Unobstructed exits are a baseline safety requirement.
[ ] Music system is active
feedback: Audio entertainment is not a safety requirement.
[x] Emergency contacts are posted
:::
::: match Match each hazard to a control {points=4 shuffle}
- Chemical splash -> Face shield
- Fall risk -> Guard rail
- Electrical fault -> Lockout/tagout
:::
::: order Put the response process in order {points=4 shuffle}
1. Stop work
2. Secure area
3. Notify supervisor
4. Document incident
:::
::: fill-blank Complete the procedure sentence {points=2}
Before restarting equipment, verify {isolation} and confirm the {permit} is active.
:::
:::

# Reflection {hideTitle}

## Reflection

::: free-response Describe one practical safety change for your team {points=5 required attempts=1}
placeholder: Mention one process change and one communication habit.
:::
